<section class="py-12 md:py-16 bg-zinc-950 border-t border-zinc-800">
    <div class="max-w-[1360px] mx-auto px-5 md:px-8 lg:px-10">
        <h2 class="text-[20px] md:text-[24px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.6px] text-white mb-8">
            Frequently asked questions (FAQ)
        </h2>
        <div class="max-w-[636px] space-y-0">
            <div class="border-b border-zinc-800 py-4">
                <button class="flex items-center justify-between w-full text-left group" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('hidden')">
                    <span class="text-base md:text-lg text-white font-medium group-hover:text-accent-lime transition-colors">Does modeling a scenario in Cortextual change the actual org?</span>
                    <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-zinc-400 group-hover:text-accent-lime transition-colors" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                        <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/>
                    </svg>
                </button>
                <div class="mt-3 text-base text-zinc-300 leading-[150%]">
                    No. Scenarios are modeled independently of your live org structure, so nothing changes until you decide to act. Plus, they are private by default and only visible to authorized users.
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="border-b border-zinc-800 py-4">
                <button class="flex items-center justify-between w-full text-left group" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('hidden')">
                    <span class="text-base md:text-lg text-white font-medium group-hover:text-accent-lime transition-colors">How many scenarios can I create?</span>
                    <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-zinc-400 group-hover:text-accent-lime transition-colors" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                        <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/>
                    </svg>
                </button>
                <div class="hidden mt-3 text-base text-zinc-300 leading-[150%]">
                    You can create as many scenarios as you need. Compare them side by side to find the optimal path forward.
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="border-b border-zinc-800 py-4">
                <button class="flex items-center justify-between w-full text-left group" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('hidden')">
                    <span class="text-base md:text-lg text-white font-medium group-hover:text-accent-lime transition-colors">Can I compare two restructuring options side by side?</span>
                    <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-zinc-400 group-hover:text-accent-lime transition-colors" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                        <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/>
                    </svg>
                </button>
                <div class="hidden mt-3 text-base text-zinc-300 leading-[150%]">
                    Yes, you can compare any two scenarios side by side, or compare any scenario against your current organization to see the full impact.
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="border-b border-zinc-800 py-4">
                <button class="flex items-center justify-between w-full text-left group" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('hidden')">
                    <span class="text-base md:text-lg text-white font-medium group-hover:text-accent-lime transition-colors">Can I see the legal and compliance exposure of a scenario?</span>
                    <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-zinc-400 group-hover:text-accent-lime transition-colors" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                        <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/>
                    </svg>
                </button>
                <div class="hidden mt-3 text-base text-zinc-300 leading-[150%]">
                    Yes, compliance risk visibility shows you the legal and compliance implications of every workforce decision alongside its cost.
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
